<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Guánica</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Guánica is a town on the south-western coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/puerto-rico">Puerto Rico</a>. On 25 July 1898, during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spanish-american-war">Spanish–American War</a>, US troops under General Nelson Miles landed there to begin the invasion of Puerto Rico. The area is known for its dry forest, a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unesco">UNESCO</a> biosphere reserve.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/guanica.jpg" alt="Guánica" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Les &amp; Omy · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Atardecer_en_San_Jacinto,_Guanica_-_panoramio.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
